=== layout: one-panel

# Summary: test inheritance models

@body

- Trace transmission across generations
- Check affected relatives and unaffected parents
- Compare transmission through males and females
- Use several clues to test an inheritance model

@notes

Treat patterns as evidence under the stated rare-allele assumptions. Small families can fit more than one model; generation skipping or sex counts alone are not proof. Ask for one decisive transmission clue.

